{
  "dom_id": "step-q175520",
  "name": "Question 15",
  "problem": "Find the truth set of $P(x)\u2227Q(x)$ given the following predicates defined over the set of positive integers:\n\n- $P(x):$ $x$ is even\n\n- $Q(x):$ $x$ is less than $9$",
  "worked_solution": "The truth set of $P(x)\u2227Q(x)$ represents the *intersection* of the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n$$\n{T}_{P\u2227Q}={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q}\n$$\n\nWe start by finding the truth sets of $P(x)$ and $Q(x):$\n\n- The truth set of $P(x)$ is the set of all even positive integers, i.e.,\n\n$$\n{T}_{P}={2,4,6,8,10,\u2026}.\n$$\n\n- The truth set of $Q(x)$ is \n\n$$\n{T}_{Q}={1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{T}_{P\u2227Q} & ={T}_{P}\\cap {T}_{Q} \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8,10,\u2026}\\cap {1,2,3,4,5,6,7,8} \\\\  & ={2,4,6,8}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
